<div class="fr-bar" role="group" aria-label="Severity filter"><button type="button" class="fr-pill" data-sev="ALL" aria-pressed="true">All</button><button type="button" class="fr-pill" data-sev="BLOCKER" aria-pressed="false">BLOCKER</button><button type="button" class="fr-pill" data-sev="HIGH" aria-pressed="false">HIGH</button><button type="button" class="fr-pill" data-sev="MED" aria-pressed="false">MED</button><button type="button" class="fr-pill" data-sev="LOW" aria-pressed="false">LOW</button><button type="button" class="fr-pill" data-sev="NIT" aria-pressed="false">NIT</button></div>
<ul class="fr-list">
<li data-sev="LOW"><details><summary><span class="fr-sev">LOW</span> T11: Paired calibration test failed once under full-suite load <code>crates/engine-cli/tests/calibrate_pair.rs:106</code> [deferred]</summary><p>a_paired_run_plays_both_arms_on_the_same_seeds_and_compares_every_band failed its exit-code assertion once during a full `cargo test --workspace` run. It passed three times on its own and in the next full run.</p><p><strong>Decision:</strong> Seen once and could not be reproduced. The cause is probably concurrent calibration workers under load. Diagnosing it needs repeated runs under load, which is not a localized fix.</p></details></li>
<li data-sev="LOW"><details><summary><span class="fr-sev">LOW</span> PERF-5: step clones the whole Tuning every tick <code>crates/engine/src/sim.rs:766</code> [deferred]</summary><p>About 0.7 KB copied ~280k times per match (1-2% of the tick budget).</p><p><strong>Decision:</strong> The fix (Arc&lt;Tuning&gt; or split borrows) touches every tuning reader and test that edits tuning in place; not localized.</p></details></li>
<li data-sev="LOW"><details><summary><span class="fr-sev">LOW</span> T6: Four acceptance tests are #[ignore] and nothing runs them <code>crates/engine/tests/ai_trailing.rs:15</code> [deferred]</summary><p>No CI config; AC-6/7/8 and the realism bands can regress with cargo test green.</p><p><strong>Decision:</strong> Needs a CI pipeline or a scheduled slow-test job: new infrastructure, not a localized change.</p></details></li>
<li data-sev="NIT"><details><summary><span class="fr-sev">NIT</span> SEC-5: Workflow evidence contains absolute local paths <code>.ai/workflows/football-manager-match-engine/:n/a</code> [deferred]</summary><p>About 189 lines of committed evidence carry C:\Users\&lt;name&gt; paths.</p><p><strong>Decision:</strong> Evidence files are generated workflow records; redacting them is outside this code diff and changes recorded evidence. Route to a redaction pass before publishing.</p></details></li>
<li data-sev="NIT"><details><summary><span class="fr-sev">NIT</span> T10: Several viewer modules have no unit tests <code>web/main.mjs:1</code> [deferred]</summary><p>main.mjs, lineup-editor.mjs, substitution-picker.mjs, socket.mjs, scoreboard.mjs, signal.mjs, launcher.mjs.</p><p><strong>Decision:</strong> Writing new suites for seven modules is broad test work, not a localized fix.</p></details></li>
<li data-sev="NIT"><details><summary><span class="fr-sev">NIT</span> M10: refusalReason parses the engine error prefix <code>web/recovery.mjs:33</code> [deferred]</summary><p>Coupled to Rust Display text by a comment only.</p><p><strong>Decision:</strong> A structured reason field crosses the engine, launcher and page contract; not localized.</p></details></li>
</ul>
<script>(function(){var root=document.currentScript.closest('.fragment-review');var pills=root.querySelectorAll('.fr-pill');pills.forEach(function(p){p.addEventListener('click',function(){var s=p.getAttribute('data-sev');pills.forEach(function(q){q.setAttribute('aria-pressed',q===p?'true':'false')});root.querySelectorAll('.fr-list li').forEach(function(li){li.hidden=!(s==='ALL'||li.getAttribute('data-sev')===s)})})});window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('sdlc:fragment-ready',{detail:{name:'review',artifact:'review',counts:{findings:6,blockers:0}}}))})();</script>
